    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="1125" n="967" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg967"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Italian
                        Chargé</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-05-15"><hi rendition="#italic">May 15,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 370.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In further reply to your note of the 24th
                    ultimo, I have the honor to inclose a copy of a letter from the Secretary of
                    Agriculture regretting that his department is unable to grant a longer period
                    than that fixed by F. I. D. 39, May 1, for the importation, without the label
                    “Artificially colored,” of Italian colored pastes.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
